{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/meetshukla_/status/2102271476950819238","id":"2102271476950819238","text":"https://x.com/i/article/2102221572660482048","raw_text":{"text":"https://t.co/nCRQ02tXxh","display_text_range":[0,23],"facets":[{"type":"url","indices":[0,23],"original":"https://t.co/nCRQ02tXxh","replacement":"https://x.com/i/article/2102221572660482048","display":"x.com/i/article/2102…"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"meetshukla_","url":"https://x.com/meetshukla_","id":"1373685139889262593","followers":929,"following":391,"likes":2380,"media_count":542,"name":"Meet Shukla","description":"Marketing apps with AI UGC at http://ghostfeed.ai","raw_description":{"text":"Marketing apps with AI UGC at https://t.co/FMAjIhWFfV","facets":[{"type":"url","indices":[30,53],"original":"https://t.co/FMAjIhWFfV","replacement":"http://ghostfeed.ai","display":"ghostfeed.ai"}]},"location":"Canada","banner_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1373685139889262593/1774291029","avatar_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1982516814308347904/u4_eSkSS_200x200.jpg","joined":"Sun Mar 21 17:17:34 +0000 2021","protected":false,"website":null,"verification":{"verified":true,"verified_at":null,"type":"individual"},"avatar_color":null},"replies":0,"retweets":2,"likes":16,"bookmarks":38,"quotes":1,"created_at":"Tue Sep 22 05:39:13 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1790055553,"possibly_sensitive":false,"views":1577,"is_note_tweet":false,"community_note":null,"lang":null,"replying_to":null,"replying_to_status":null,"source":"Twitter Web App","article":{"created_at":"2026-09-22T05:39:13.000Z","modified_at":"2026-09-22T05:39:13.000Z","id":"2102221572660482048","title":"How to generate 1000s of AI UGC reactions to flood your ugc accounts","preview_text":"Over the last six months, people imported more than 10,000 videos into Ghostfeed. We handpicked 1,066 references from that pile. I wanted to use them to make new videos with different creators, but","cover_media":{"id":"QXBpTWVkaWE6DAAFCgABHSzEYz5WwAAKAAITEE9bTFUQAQAA","media_id":"2102271056601858048","media_info":{"__typename":"ApiImage","color_info":{"palette":[{"percentage":61.78,"rgb":{"blue":20,"green":21,"red":22}},{"percentage":16.71,"rgb":{"blue":104,"green":114,"red":155}},{"percentage":12.15,"rgb":{"blue":117,"green":125,"red":134}},{"percentage":12.09,"rgb":{"blue":180,"green":196,"red":202}},{"percentage":1.26,"rgb":{"blue":39,"green":90,"red":185}}]},"original_img_height":669,"original_img_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSzEYz5WwAAZyuw.jpg","original_img_width":1672},"media_key":"3_2102271056601858048"},"content":{"blocks":[{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"6kgm","text":"Over the last six months, people imported more than 10,000 videos into Ghostfeed. We handpicked 1,066 references from that pile. I wanted to use them to make new videos with different creators, but first I needed a better way to find the right reference.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"1ke60","text":"So this weekend I ran video understanding on the library. The goal was simple: tell me what happens in each video, what structure it follows, and what reaction the person shows. Gemini handled the video analysis. The replay below shows those saved results being sorted.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":0,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"8kbbj","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"a7j52","text":"Once we know the structure, we know which workflow to use","type":"header-one"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"bi9r7","text":"I gave the analysis fixed choices: reaction, lip-sync, hook + demo, talking head, and B-roll. The reaction is a separate label, such as shocked, confused, or angry. That means I can look for a particular performance instead of scrolling through a category like “beauty.”","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"bc00d","text":"For reaction and lip-sync, I use motion-based cloning in Ghostfeed. I want to change the creator while using the source performance as the reference. For B-roll and talking head, I use prompt-based cloning to make a new version from the scene and structure.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"30v61","text":"Hook + demo is where I combine the pieces. I clone the opening, then add my product demo in the editor. I do not need to recreate an entire reference video to use its opening.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"744mt","text":"Here is what motion-based cloning can do","type":"header-one"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"a0h4","text":"I choose the reference and the creator I want to use in Ghostfeed, then use Wan 3 Smart Motion for the motion-based clone. Here are two examples we made, with the source and the new versions shown together.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"78cem","text":"The first is a crying reaction. What I wanted to keep was the expression: the eyes, the mouth, and the small changes in the face. The comparison shows that performance on different creators. This is the kind of opening I would choose when the text needs a sad or upset reaction.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":1,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"b0c81","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"73mfk","text":"The second is a mirror lip-sync clip. Here I want the mouth movement and the hand gestures to follow the source performance. The comparison changes the creator and appearance while keeping the mirror framing and the movement recognizable. For a clip like this, I watch it with the audio before choosing the version to use.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":2,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"e7c74","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"acbrt","text":"Turn the outputs into posts","type":"header-one"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"3a6f","text":"These clips give me the opening. Next I take one into the Ghostfeed editor, add the hook text, and place my product footage after it. I trim the transition so the demo follows what the opening promises.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"496n7","text":"Once that edit works, I can make versions with another creator, another first line, or a different product angle. That is how I would build a batch for Instagram and TikTok, then export the finished videos together.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"7763t","text":"The library is live with 1,066 references. Find the structure, choose the workflow, and make your version in Ghostfeed.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":3,"length":39,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"def4v","text":"Browse the reaction inspiration library","type":"unstyled"}],"entityMap":[{"key":"0","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"e25131d0-3c71-4948-a882-a321333b21cf","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"5","mediaCategory":"AmplifyVideo","mediaId":"2102228915875926017"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"1","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"1021054b-d8d3-4f1f-a703-6a9b977629b2","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"8","mediaCategory":"AmplifyVideo","mediaId":"2102232819078402048"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"2","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"a4b04f92-779f-441c-b68a-ec73278c1828","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"4","mediaCategory":"AmplifyVideo","mediaId":"2102252079590912000"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"3","value":{"data":{"url":"https://ghostfeed.ai/tools/reaction-inspiration-library"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"LINK"}}]},"media_entities":[{"id":"QXBpTWVkaWE6DAAECgABHSyeD5dW0AEKAAIAAAAAAAAAAAAA","media_id":"2102228915875926017","media_info":{"__typename":"ApiVideo","aspect_ratio":{"denominator":9,"numerator":16},"duration_millis":26000,"preview_image":{"color_info":{"palette":[{"percentage":94.37,"rgb":{"blue":236,"green":243,"red":246}},{"percentage":2.72,"rgb":{"blue":103,"green":114,"red":117}},{"percentage":1.53,"rgb":{"blue":63,"green":64,"red":72}},{"percentage":0.48,"rgb":{"blue":131,"green":158,"red":208}},{"percentage":0.41,"rgb":{"blue":227,"green":199,"red":231}}]},"original_img_height":1080,"original_img_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2102228915875926017/img/rJi7r3eykz0YHvHz.jpg","original_img_width":1920},"variants":[{"bit_rate":256000,"content_type":"video/mp4","url":"https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2102228915875926017/vid/avc1/480x270/fVmP5PcA7tG0HzSG.mp4?tag=29"},{"bit_rate":10368000,"content_type":"video/mp4","url":"https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2102228915875926017/vid/avc1/1920x1080/jGvaJihzdO2Lah7b.mp4?tag=29"},{"content_type":"application/x-mpegURL","url":"https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2102228915875926017/pl/zOGWclnr-VUayN5w.m3u8?tag=29"},{"bit_rate":832000,"content_type":"video/mp4","url":"https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2102228915875926017/vid/avc1/640x360/q-ESj11CleDUbh-y.mp4?tag=29"},{"bit_rate":2176000,"content_type":"video/mp4","url":"https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2102228915875926017/vid/avc1/1280x720/k2LE-7qV0JUtPEqd.mp4?tag=29"}]},"media_key":"13_2102228915875926017"},{"id":"QXBpTWVkaWE6DAAECgABHSyhnGBWEAAKAAIAAAAAAAAAAAAA","media_id":"2102232819078402048","media_info":{"__typename":"ApiVideo","aspect_ratio":{"denominator":120,"numerator":203},"duration_millis":5000,"preview_image":{"color_info":{"palette":[{"percentage":47.14,"rgb":{"blue":15,"green":16,"red":14}},{"percentage":29.14,"rgb":{"blue":123,"green":142,"red":176}},{"percentage":8.89,"rgb":{"blue":144,"green":77,"red":44}},{"perce